xnu: MERLIN 0122 remove the boot-screen Apple mark (default off)

The 0120 mark (Simple Icons outline) reads as a knock-off on the real
panel and the user asked it removed.  0122 gates the whole mark path in
sweet_boot_ui_start() behind a new boot-arg, sweetbootui_logo, which
defaults to 0:

  - bootui.mask stays NULL, so bootui_blit_logo() no-ops via its own
    NULL guard and bootui_rasterize_mask() returns before touching it;
  - everything else is untouched: the one-time black clear, the real
    milestone progress bar (root mount / launchd / backboardd /
    SpringBoard / first composited frame), panic protection, console
    muting, the frame-feedback handover, and the mask free race-safety
    from the 0120 review (the free still happens only when a mask was
    actually allocated);
  - boot-arg sweetbootui_logo=1 restores the 0120 behaviour in full;
    sweetbootui=0 still disables the whole boot screen.

No other file changes.  Verified by host-compile of SweetBootUI.cpp
(-DSWEET -DSWEET_BOOTUI_HOST_TEST) plus a host behaviour test: with the
default args the mark region stays black at every redraw while the bar
fills with the milestones.

